# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore` rather than `.dockerignore`: the build context is the
# repository root, so a `backend/.dockerignore` would be ignored entirely. BuildKit (which
# Compose v2 uses by default) looks for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` first, which
# keeps this rule set next to the Dockerfile it belongs to instead of at the repo root,
# where it would collide with the other workspaces' owners.
# Paths below are relative to the repository root.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.git
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/coverage
planning
scripts/local
frontend/dist
.claude
